UID:e87bed03bb4e890e@role-employment-labor.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261027T221053Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] US Department of Labor finds none of nation
 ’s 12\,000 mining operations met criteria for pattern of violations in f
 iscal year 2026
DESCRIPTION:WASHINGTON – The U.S. Department of Labor’s Mine Safety a
 nd Health Administration announced today that none of the nation’s 12\,0
 00 mining operations met the criteria for a pattern of violations notice\,
  one of the agency’s toughest enforcement tools.In MSHA’s annual scree
 ning of operations from Oct. 1\, 2025\, to Sept. 30\, 2026\, the agency f
 ound no pattern of violation notices. The Federal Mine Safety and Health A
 ct of 1977 includes the pattern of violations provision for mines with a r
 ecurring pattern of significant and substantial violations – those that 
 are reasonably likely to result in a serious injury or illness – and oth
 er safety and health compliance problems. If a mine receives subsequent S&
 S violations after being placed on POV\, MSHA is authorized to withdraw mi
 ners from the affected area of the mine.“Under this administration MSHA 
 remains committed to objectively calling balls and strikes in enforcement\
 , including issuing POV notices when warranted\,” said Assistant Secreta
 ry for Mine Safety and Health Wayne D. Palmer. “For the third year in a
  row\, no mine received a POV notice which\, combined with the lowest-ever
  all-injury rate in 2025\, signals continued progress toward protecting mi
 ners from safety and health hazards.”MSHA provides mine operators with o
 nline tools to help monitor compliance. The POV calculator allows mine op
 erators to monitor performance under the POV screening criteria and alerts
  mine operators that corrective actions are needed. The agency’s S&S ca
 lculator enables mine operators to monitor their “significant and substa
 ntial” violations. It is the responsibility of mine operators to track 
 their violation and injury histories to determine whether they need to tak
 e action to avoid meeting the POV screening criteria. Learn more about M
 SHA.\nhttp://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/msha/msha20261027
URL:http://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/msha/msha20261027
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
